          equipment: '162-card deck (or special Canastone cards with red/black discs), score sheet',
          dealing: 'Partnerships by drawing cards (highest vs lowest). Dealer gives 15 cards each. Next card turned up starts discard pile (pozzo). If 3 or wild, keep turning until natural found. If first 3 all wild/3s, redeal. Dealer adds face-down packet to discard pile: size = rank of face-up card (Ace=14, King=13, ..., Four=4). If face-up 2 or joker, pile is frozen (turned sideways). Stock pile (tallone) is remaining cards.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points by forming melds and canastas. Special bonuses for wild card canastas and Ace canastas. Be first team to complete required canastas and go out.',
          gameplay: "Red 3s: placed face up before play, replaced with new cards. Opening (team's first meld): Can only be done at START of turn before drawing. Requirements: 50+ pts if team score <3000; 90+ pts if 3000-5000; 120+ pts if >5000. Opening player continues with normal turn. Before opening: draw 2 from stock, meld any red 3s drawn (replaced), discard 1 to end turn. After opening: draw either (a) 2 from stock, OR (b) entire discard pile + 1 from stock. Then may meld, then discard. Melds: 3+ cards same rank. Natural melds: max 2 wild cards (must have more naturals than wilds). Canasta: 7+ card meld. Clean (pulito): no wilds. Dirty (sporco): has wilds. Wild card meld: commits team to complete 7+ wild canasta; cannot use wilds elsewhere until completed. Special canastas: Wild canasta clean = all 2s or all 6 jokers+1 two; dirty = 1-5 jokers+2s. Ace canasta: 7+ aces. Threes: red 3s score separately; black 3s can only be discarded, never melded. Frozen pile: if has wild or black 3 on top, can only take if have 2 natural cards of same rank as top card in hand.",
          keyRules: [
            '162 cards: 3 decks + 6 jokers',
            '4 players in partnerships (or 6 in two teams of 3)',
            '15 cards dealt each',
            'Discard pile starts with variable face-down cards (4-14 based on turned card)',
            'Opening meld only at start of turn',
            'Draw: 2 from stock OR discard pile + 1 from stock',
            'Wild card meld commits team to complete it',
            'Special canastas: Wild (clean/dirty), Aces',
            'Red 3s placed before play; black 3s only discards',
            'Frozen pile requires 2 naturals to take',
            'Target: 10000 points',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on making your opening meld as soon as possible. Decide whether to draw 2 from stock or take the discard pile based on what you need. Start canastas early so you can go out later.',
          intermediate: 'Coordinate with partner on which canastas to pursue. The wild card canasta is valuable (2000 pts clean) but commits you - only start if you have many wilds. Track red 3s - having 4 is great (1000 pts), but 5 is bad (-600 penalty). Manage the discard pile - taking it gives many cards but may include unwanted points.',
          advanced: 'Complex decisions about when to take the large initial discard pile. Timing your go-out to maximize bonuses or minimize opponent opportunities. Strategic freezing of the discard pile. Optimal allocation of wild cards between natural melds vs wild canasta attempt.',
          tips: [
            'Taking the initial discard pile can give 15+ cards - evaluate carefully',
            'Wild canasta clean (all 2s or 6 jokers+1 two) = 2000 points',
            'Avoid having exactly 5 red 3s (-600 penalty) or 6 (-1000)',
            'Black 3s are safe discards that freeze the pile',
            'Opening meld requirements increase as your score increases',
            "Coordinate with partner - don't both work on same rank",
            'Ace canasta (1000 pts) is easier than wild canasta',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
